A||||4||RobH||What "filter" is this?||||5||
Z||000000||RobH||06-14-2000||09:43 PM||||Sorry I don't have a pic, but hopefully I can describe it well enough...here goes...<P>It is about 1.5 inches diameter, right in the middle on the firewall in the engine compartment.  Hose from top of "filter" runs to black tube into plenum, hose on bottom of "filter" runs through the firewall.  I assume it has something to do with emissions, but not sure.<P>I've looked in my Helms Service Manual and Haynes book, but can't find any references to this.  What is it?<P>BTW, I have a 2.8L V6 and am in the process of rebuilding it, so I thought I'd replace all hoses, vacuum lines, etc.<P>Thanks...<BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||06-14-2000||10:12 PM||||Brake booster filter. Not all years have them. I don't know if they are replaceable or not. Seems like I heard they were not.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobH||06-14-2000||10:26 PM||||Fiero56 --<P>Thanks...that is it.  I just looked it up in the Helms manual, and there it is!  According to the manual, it can be replaced, but not sure that I need too.<P>The hoses are not clamped to the filter, so I am wondering if this has been any help at all (since it may not have sealed properly). What diff should I notice if this is working vs not working?<P>Thanks again.<BR>Rob||||reg||10
Z||000003||ka4nkf||06-14-2000||11:34 PM||||THIS is the brake booster filter and it is located in a spot where it gets a lot of heat therfore it is plastic and gets brittle and It will leak vac. If you have several miles on the car I would replace it or best of all elimate it because it is not necessary. I dont think the 88 models use it.just take it out and put a pice of tubing conector in between , you can get thes straight connectors at the hardware store in the pvc fittings department.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||06-15-2000||05:09 AM||||I believe they stopped putting the filters on in 87.  You don't need it, anyways.  take it out and throw it away..||||reg||1
